                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Thu Nguyen",
                        "email": "thu@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "ThuBaNguyen"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we apply the changing for this code https://github.com/openbmc/pldm/blob/366507c82a4781c4a893ab9b9ca7b38f2157a353/platform-mc/terminus_manager.cpp#L530"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "Here we are doing a reinterpret cast, which means you're treating the memory address of supportedTypes as a pointer to a bitfield8_t object. This is low-level type-punning, essentially reinterpreting the memory layout of supportedTypes to treat it as a different type.\nbut \nPlacement new is used to construct an object in an already-allocated memory location. It does not allocate memory, but rather constructs an object at a specified location.\n\nWe could convert this to use placement new, but I think its better to use a cast here."
                }
            ],
